 * type: module
 * part-of: foah
 * exports: [run, checkConstraints]
 * description: "The stepping map γ_t for constraint evaluation. Loads the precompiled constraint cache, evaluates tool calls against constraint patterns, returns allow/block. This is the thin hook adapter — all logic lives in constraint entity fibers."
 * ---
 *
 * Hook adapter for PreToolUse. Reads the constraint cache (not the full graph),
 * tests the tool input against constraint regexes, returns exit code 0 (allow)
 * or 2 (block).
 *
 * Four-layer architecture:
 *   Entity fibers (constraint .md files) → WHAT to check
 *   Precompiled cache (constraints.json) → fast-lookup format
 *   This file (stepping map γ_t) → HOW to check
 *   Hook registration in settings.json → WHEN to check
 */
"use strict";

